-- ============================================================================
-- EC3 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Probabilistic Economics, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: ONE SCREENING CASE AND ITS RANGE. What a screening
-- model is and refuses (mid-year discounting, a fixed 20 year quick life, no
-- economic limit, TaxRoyalty only in the quick form, no PIA terms); the quick
-- inputs expanded into a case (a decline taken year on year, capex split over
-- two years, fixed and variable opex, a flat price); the royalty and tax
-- ledger; NPV row by row, payback part way through a year, IRR by Newton and
-- peak exposure; and one number becoming three through the sensitivity sweep,
-- a two-sided tornado and Low, Base and High scenarios.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. The screening engine has NO ECONOMIC
-- LIMIT: every year of the quick form's 20 year life is produced and charged,
-- so late years whose opex outruns revenue still lower the value. A reader
-- who assumes the model stops producing when a year loses money reads every
-- late row wrong.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The sensitivity sweep scales fixed opex
-- only and scales oil volume without the variable opex that follows it, and
-- a scenario moves four inputs at once. Both are one number moved by a
-- stated rule, not a distribution, and the tier ends by saying so.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the ledger
-- columns and the deterministic value measures.
-- ============================================================================

values ('uncertainty', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-screening-model-is","title":"What a Screening Model Is","lesson_keys":["l01-one-number-is-a-guess","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses-to-be","l04-the-units-that-travel"]},{"key":"m02-the-case-before-the-numbers","title":"The Case Before the Numbers","lesson_keys":["l01-quick-inputs-and-a-fixed-life","l02-a-decline-year-on-year","l03-capex-over-two-years","l04-fixed-and-variable-opex","l05-a-price-that-never-moves"]},{"key":"m03-the-royalty-and-tax-ledger","title":"The Royalty and Tax Ledger","lesson_keys":["l01-gross-revenue-in-millions","l02-royalty-off-the-top","l03-taxable-income-and-expensing","l04-tax-only-on-a-positive-base","l05-net-cash-flow"]},{"key":"m04-value-from-a-ledger","title":"Value from a Ledger","lesson_keys":["l01-mid-year-discounting","l02-npv-row-by-row","l03-payback-part-way-through-a-year","l04-irr-by-newton","l05-peak-exposure"]},{"key":"m05-one-number-becomes-three","title":"One Number Becomes Three","lesson_keys":["l01-the-sensitivity-sweep","l02-a-tornado-has-two-sides","l03-low-base-and-high","l04-what-a-scenario-is-not"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'uncertainty' and tier = 'beginner';

